    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 18 slate with a heavy emphasis on high-upside speed, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who carries our highest daily efficiency score of 77.20. His matchup against Taj Bradley is exceptional, buoyed by a +14% platoon advantage and a +4% boost for Bradley\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to weaponize his elite sprint speed. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (70.38) remains an automatic start at leadoff against Manaea, benefiting from a +10% order stability bonus and wind conditions providing a +5% lift to his power profile. While **Yordan Alvarez** (68.98) faces a challenging lefty-lefty matchup, his elite 0.475 xwOBA overrides the platoon suppression, keeping him firmly in the lineup over bench alternatives.\n\nOur rotation strategy prioritized efficiency over raw volume, forcing a difficult call on **Casey Schmitt** (48.22). While **Casey Schmitt** offers a +11% dynamic platoon boost against Woo, his overall profile lacked the ceiling of our middle-of-the-order anchors like **Colt Keith** (68.51). **Colt Keith**\u2019s projection remains elevated due to his high-leverage spot in the lineup, making him a safer play than the marginal scores seen at the bottom of our active roster. We are closely monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (51.69) and **Colt Keith**\u2014both remain listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" Should their assumed #3 spots shift, we may see a minor volatility adjustment in their floor, but their skill-based projections against the 5.30 xERA of Rodriguez should hold their value regardless of minor order movement. We continue to keep **Carson Benge** on the bench, as his sub-40 efficiency score against Luzardo failed to clear our internal floor, ensuring our limited plate appearances are allocated to high-percentage outcomes.",
